WEBVTT

00:00:00.088 --> 00:00:03.288
Expand Advanced Automation and open Workflows.

00:00:03.675 --> 00:00:06.975
Read the description and select the service actually available.

00:00:07.388 --> 00:00:12.500
Integrated Foundation Central, standalone F C A and classic Foundation

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.625
V M use different contracts.

00:00:15.025 --> 00:00:19.825
Import or complete the matching form and review its generated configuration.

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:24.162
Do not assume that a similarly named action has the same credentials

00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:25.725
or execution semantics.

00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:32.017
Open Scripts for a specific allowlisted action Use its parameter wizard and

00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:37.004
installed schema then review the generated input A script sequence and a

00:00:37.004 --> 00:00:42.042
workflow are different launch modes Supply the required saved file and

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:47.174
inspect verification after execution Set Prism Login Title for P

00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:52.354
E is now available as a focused script or pipeline action with title-only

00:00:52.354 --> 00:00:57.229
Configure Cluster support Review the exact title and cluster select the

00:00:57.229 --> 00:01:01.692
correct vault credential reference and retain certificate verification The

00:01:01.692 --> 00:01:06.767
action compares the existing setting applies a change only when needed and

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:11.779
requires a fresh readback to verify the requested title Legacy U

00:01:11.779 --> 00:01:17.037
I A P I compatibility still needs validation against the target

00:01:17.104 --> 00:01:22.142
A O S version A saved title or subprocess success alone does not

00:01:22.142 --> 00:01:23.812
prove the target displays it

00:01:24.221 --> 00:01:27.883
For local P E users choose Create Local Users for P E.

00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:32.158
Each requested username needs its own matching credential reference.

00:01:32.571 --> 00:01:36.683
Select the intended role set explicitly and respect the installed

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:37.233
schema.

00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:39.421
Run Dry Run before submission.

00:01:39.821 --> 00:01:43.833
After creation, independently confirm that each account is enabled

00:01:44.146 --> 00:01:47.483
and has both Cluster Admin and User Admin when those are the

00:01:47.483 --> 00:01:48.421
approved roles.

00:01:49.587 --> 00:01:54.300
Inspect the stage and safe category when local user creation fails.

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:59.725
Credential resolution, certificate trust, identity mismatch, network

00:01:59.737 --> 00:02:04.513
access, creation, role assignment and verification are separate failure

00:02:04.513 --> 00:02:05.037
points.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.650
Check whether any accounts or roles were already created.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:13.663
Correct the actual cause and rerun only through the supported process.

00:02:14.063 --> 00:02:18.300
Do not paste passwords or raw authentication headers into a support

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:18.887
request.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.825
The C V M and Dell i D R A C rotation

00:02:23.837 --> 00:02:27.475
workflow has a separate support boundary and exact confirmations.

00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:32.575
Verify each C V M host-key fingerprint independently, establish the

00:02:32.575 --> 00:02:36.087
required access and keep an out-of-band recovery path.

00:02:36.487 --> 00:02:42.225
Review any manual follow-up, including host I P M I credential synchronization.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.750
A dry run or approval does not prove that live rotation is

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.925
validated for your firmware and release.
